{
  "raw": {
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3978627": {
      "title": "Residence Hall Director",
      "description": "Residence Hall Director. Elizabethtown College. Description Residence Life at Elizabethtown College invites applications for Residence Hall Director . The primary purpose of this position is to lead and oversee a neighborhood of residential communities (traditional halls, apartments, on-campus houses, and/or quads) to ensure a healthy and vibrant community. This position is considered an essential employee during inclement weather and other unexpected emergency events. This position is a 12 month, live-on campus role, with nights as weekends as necessary. For full consideration please provide cover letter, resume, and contact information for three (3) references when applying. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: SUPERVISION Recruit, hire, train, and supervise student staff (such as senior resident assistants, resident assistants, and/or community assistants) Assist with the recruitment, selection, and training of student leaders in Residence Life Supervise student leaders through weekly one-on-one meetings, team meetings, and as needed coaching and development plans and evaluations HOUSING & RESIDENCE LIFE, COMMUNITY LIVING, AND STUDENT LIFE Housing Coordination, Assignments, and Facilities Oversight, awareness, and attention of the entirety of your neighborhood to ensure that students have holistic support Assist with housing selection and assignments Coordinate room changes for students in your residential communities as needed Assist with break stay and exception requests Open and close buildings Communicate with parents and family members of students that have questions about anything related to their residential experience and find solutions to any issues Oversee and conduct health and safety inspections each semester Complete monthly building walkthroughs Collaborate with Facilities and Environmental Services to be included in the solutions of ongoing or consistent issues or concerns On-Call, Crisis Management, and Student Rights and Responsibilities Participate in the Administrator On-Call (AOC) rotation Be familiar with established emergency protocols, and be prepared to implement them when necessary Partner with Campus Safety to ensure smooth responses and shared expectations to situations involving officers and Residence Life Communicate, monitor, and enforce College policies and procedures Adjudicate conduct cases as assigned Perform wellness checks, advise and refer students to appropriate resources Participate in Bias or Title IX investigations or hearing panels as needed General Duties within Division and Department Demonstrate an active commitment to fostering vibrant communities and a sense of belonging for students Monitor and respond to emails in the shared Residence Life department inbox Assist with social media posts for Residence Life Assist with all trainings/workshops, recruitment and selection, community programming, and housing selection processes and events Participate in signature campus events such as New Student Orientation (NSO), Admissions Open Houses and Accepted Student Days, Homecoming and Family Weekend, and TGIS Dine with students, faculty, and staff in college dining facilities using available meal plan Other duties as assigned ASSESSMENT Participate in departmental assessment initiatives Visit weekly with students to learn how their experience is progressing and amplify those things that are value added, while seeking solutions for those that are issues Partner with Academics, Athletics, Student Assembly, Alumni Relations, SAAC, and peer mentors to leverage existing experiences and amplify their impact Solicit input and sample students from across campus in both survey and focus group formats Qualifications To perform this position successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential function satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made. Required Qualifications: Reside in assigned college-owned housing Bachelor’s degree required; plus, two years of relevant experience; or equivalent combination of education and experience Previous supervisory experience preferred Other Skills, Abilities, and/or Training Ability to work extended hours Ability to work nights and weekends Ability to preserve confidentiality of information Ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Ability to work within strict deadlines Good interpersonal skills and desire to be a team player Exceptional customer service skills Excellent communication skills Sense of creativity and curiosity Ability to use Microsoft Teams phone system Proficient with Microsoft Office Suite Ability to use StarRez Elizabethtown College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by state or federal law."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4557427": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty -Teaching First Semester Biology Laboratory",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty -Teaching First Semester Biology Laboratory. Elizabethtown College. Description The School of Sciences & Health at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking an Adjunct Faculty-Teaching First Semester Biology Laboratory for the spring semester. The successful applicant will teach one laboratory section (3 work units) of a first semester biology course (Biology 111L) for science majors for the Elizabethtown College Department of Biological and Environmental Sciences. Position Responsibilities are as follows: Teach the laboratory course in person using an existing Canvas course, including laboratory protocols, assignments and exams. Meet regularly with the Biology 111 laboratory course coordinator and the department co-chairs to discuss course progress. Work with a undergraduate laboratory assistant recruited and trained by the Biology 111 laboratory course coordinator. Mentor the students in the classroom and seek help as necessary with concerns about students. Be open to classroom peer evaluation Maintain regularly scheduled in-person office hours Applicants should have an MS degree or Ph.D. in a biological field of study or should be in the process of obtaining a Ph.D. For full consideration please provide cover letter, CV or resume, and contact information for 3 references. Please note, Elizabethtown College is not sponsoring visas for this position and is only considering US citizens for this position at this time. Requirements"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4559540": {
      "title": "Financial Services Assistant",
      "description": "Financial Services Assistant. Elizabethtown College. Description The Office of Financial Aid at Elizabethtown College is currently accepting applications for a Financial Services Assistant. The primary purpose of the Financial Services Assistant is to support the Office of Financial Aid in recruiting and retaining students through responsive service to students and families, accurate administrative support, and effective data processing and analysis. The position works closely with students, families, and College staff and may assist with other office(s) functions as assigned. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Serve as the primary receiver for all incoming phone calls, appointments and walk-ins, and emails, etc. Provide welcoming, responsive service to students and their families, answering questions clearly, addressing concerns with care, and connecting them with the appropriate resources Maintain confidentiality and discretion Oversee mailing operations for Office of Financial Aid; as assigned Work closely with the Office of Marketing & Communications on communication to stakeholders as assigned Provide general information about federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs, regulations, and procedures for applying for financial aid Maintain filing system including the purging and shredding of student files after the mandatory retention period Keep track and order materials as needed Assist with Enrollment Management Division College events such as Workshops, Open Houses, Accepted Student Days, and Orientations Assist with the Federal Perkins Loan and Federal Work Study programs as needed Assist with generating and printing first award letter packages for mailing Assist the Director in reviewing reports and surveys for data accuracy Keep abreast of Title IV regulations, along with state and institutional policies and procedures Maintain working knowledge of the general services provided by Student Accounts, Registration, Academic Advising, and Admissions to respond to inquiries appropriately and accurately Perform Quality Assurance checks of student aid files to ensure accuracy and compliance Review and prepare students’ files for aid packaging Maintain and update the office Daily and Workflow calendars and the Policies and Procedures manual (electronic and paper) Manage the team functions: coverage; appointments; office purchases; and reconciling the office budget Post withdrawal dates and send required exit counseling materials Provide administrative and student service support to other College offices as assigned. Manage multiple tasks and competing priorities while meeting deadlines and maintaining accuracy Other duties as assigned Requirements To perform this position successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential function satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made. Education and/or Experience High school diploma is required; plus, two years of administrative experience. Previous Financial Aid experience is desired. Certificates, Licenses, and/or Registrations This position requires a valid driver’s license for business travel purposes."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4541486": {
      "title": "Volunteer Strength and Conditioning Intern",
      "description": "Volunteer Strength and Conditioning Intern. Elizabethtown College. Description The Athletic Department at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking a Volunteer Strength and Conditioning Intern. The Volunteer Strength and Conditioning Intern will assist with the development and delivery of training programs for NCAA Division III student-athletes. This educational opportunity provides hands-on experience in collegiate strength and conditioning, athlete monitoring, and performance testing under the supervision of the strength and conditioning staff. The individual will mentor, motivate, and develop student athletes in a Division III educational environment, and assist the Head S&C Coach to ensure the S&C program is conducted in accordance with the NCAA and conference rules and regulations. Requirements: Currently pursuing or recently completed a degree in exercise science, kinesiology, strength and conditioning, or a related field. Interest in pursuing a career in strength and conditioning or sports performance. Strong communication, organization, and interpersonal skills. Willingness to learn, accept feedback, and work collaboratively. Availability for an agreed-upon schedule, which may include early mornings or afternoons. Previous experience in a weight-room or athletic setting is preferred. Current CPR, AED, and First Aid certification is preferred. Interest in pursuing the NSCA-CSCS or CSCCa-SCCC certification is preferred. For full consideration, please provide cover letter, resume & contact information for (3) references. Please include your availability, preferred internship dates, and whether you are seeking academic credit. ACT153 are required for this position, if you have the following clearances (PA Child Abuse, PA State Police and FBI) please include them when applying. If not, the College will order them for you if an offer of employment is extended."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4534405": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Industry & Career Advising (STEM)",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Industry & Career Advising (STEM). Elizabethtown College. Description The Career Development Center at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking an Assistant Director of Industry and Career Advising (STEM). This position serves as the Career Development Center's primary liaison and subject-matter resource for the School of Engineering and Computer Science and traditional science majors in the School of Sciences and Health, delivering an integrated approach to career advising, employer engagement, experiential learning, and career readiness. The Assistant Director of Industry and Career Advising for STEM career communities, provides discipline-specific expertise while ensuring equitable, high-quality career development support for students across the institution. In this role, the Assistant Director partners closely with faculty, staff, employers, alumni, and campus stakeholders to align career development efforts with academic curricula and industry needs. The position blends individualized career advising, proactive employer and alumni engagement, and leadership in campus-wide career readiness initiatives, including the Career Action Plan, First Destination outcomes, and integration of NACE career competencies into the student experience. The Assistant Director contributes to division-wide strategy and continuous improvement efforts, supporting institutional goals related to student success, post-graduate outcomes, and workforce readiness. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Career Advising & Industry Expertise Serve as the primary Career Development Center liaison and subject-matter resource for School of Engineering and Computer Science and traditional science majors in the School of Sciences and Health, maintaining expertise in career pathways, recruiting practices and timelines, employment trends, emerging roles, professional associations, skills, credentials, and experiential learning opportunities. Provide comprehensive career advising and coaching to students related to career exploration and decision-making, career readiness, professional skill development, networking, job and internship searches, and post-graduate planning. Serve as the instructor for the School of Engineering and Computer Science professional development course, delivering career readiness curriculum aligned with School and Career Development Center priorities. Partner with faculty and staff to develop and deliver discipline- and industry-specific career resources, programming, classroom presentations, and experiential learning opportunities. Connect students with employers, alumni, graduate/professional programs, and relevant career opportunities through targeted programming, communications, Handshake, and other Career Development Center resources. Ensure consistent and equitable access to career development support across assigned areas and serve as a back-up advisor for other Schools, majors, and industries as needed. Employer, Alumni, and Experiential Engagement Develop and sustain relationships with employers, alumni, and industry professionals within assigned areas through proactive outreach, networking, site visits, referrals, conferences, and other strategic engagement. Identify and cultivate internships, employment, job shadowing, project-based learning, mentorship, site visits, and other experiential opportunities aligned with student and institutional needs. Oversee and coordinate the School of Engineering and Computer Science internship program, including administration and student support in partnership with ECS faculty and staff. Partner with campus stakeholders and faculty to expand regional and national employer and alumni engagement. Plan and execute employer-facing programs and recruiting initiatives, including industry-specific Meet and Greets, information sessions, site visits, and on-campus recruitment activities. Monitor industry trends, hiring practices, recruiting timelines, workforce needs, emerging occupations, and employer expectations; translate insights into advising, programming, faculty partnerships, and career readiness initiatives. Document employer and alumni engagement and partnership activity within designated Career Development Center systems to support coordinated outreach, assessment, and relationship management. Collaborate closely with internship directors, clinical coordinators, fieldwork coordinators, faculty, and other academic partners within assigned Schools to support students pursuing internships and other experiential learning opportunities, recognizing and leveraging their discipline-specific expertise. Campus Career Ecosystem & Outcomes Advance the Elizabethtown College Career Action Plan within assigned areas by monitoring student engagement and using participation data to inform targeted outreach, programming, and continuous improvement. Partner with Institutional Research and campus stakeholders to support First Destination Survey data collection and analysis and identify opportunities to strengthen post-graduate outcomes. Collaborate with faculty and campus partners to integrate NACE career competencies, career readiness initiatives, and emerging credentialing or digital badging frameworks into the student experience. Develop partnerships with student organizations, academic departments, alumni, and employers and curate industry-specific resources to expand career education and industry engagement. Contribute to assessment, strategic planning, and continuous improvement efforts supporting Career Development Center and institutional priorities. Career Development Center Leadership & Operations Provide leadership for assigned Center-wide programs, initiatives, technologies, or functional areas based on departmental needs and areas of expertise. Collaborate with Career Development Center colleagues to ensure consistent service delivery, share industry knowledge, cross-train across assigned areas, and support Center-wide events and initiatives. Represent the Career Development Center on institutional committees, working groups, and initiatives and contribute to the training and supervision of student employees, interns, or Career Peers as assigned. Requirements Education and/or Experience MA or MS in Higher Ed Administration, MA or MS in Counseling or similar degree Career technology: Handshake or comparable career-services management/recruiting platforms Data and workflow tools: Microsoft Excel and Airtable or comparable database/project-management tools Career-readiness technology: Big Interview or comparable virtual interviewing/career-preparation platforms Learning management systems: Canvas or comparable LMS Productivity/collaboration: Microsoft 365, particularly Outlook, Teams, Word, PowerPoint, and Excel Virtual engagement: Zoom and/or Microsoft Teams Preferred Qualifications: A minimum of three years in Career Services, Employer Relations, and/or Alumni Relations Certificates, Licenses, and/or Registrations This position requires a valid driver’s license for business travel purposes (individual must have a US driver’s license for at least three years; a motor vehicle record check will be run and the incumbent must pass the College’s MVR rating system). For full consideration please provide cover letter, resume and contact information for (3) references."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4534430": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Industry & Career Advising (Arts, Humanities & Public Service)",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Industry & Career Advising (Arts, Humanities & Public Service). Elizabethtown College. Description The Career Development Center at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking an Assistant Director of Industry and Career Advising (Arts, Humanities & Public Service). This position serves as the Career Development Center's primary liaison and subject-matter resource for the School of Public Service and School of Arts and Humanities delivering an integrated approach to career advising, employer engagement, experiential learning, and career readiness. Each Assistant Director provides discipline-specific expertise while ensuring equitable, high-quality career development support for students across the institution. In this role, the Assistant Director partners closely with faculty, staff, employers, alumni, and campus stakeholders to align career development efforts with academic curricula and industry needs. The position blends individualized career advising, proactive employer and alumni engagement, and leadership in campus-wide career readiness initiatives, including the Career Action Plan, First Destination outcomes, and integration of NACE career competencies into the student experience. In addition, this role will instruct the Career Development Center’s CP 141 Mapping Career Goals course each semester. The Assistant Director contributes to division-wide strategy and continuous improvement efforts, supporting institutional goals related to student success, post-graduate outcomes, and workforce readiness. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Career Advising & Industry Expertise Serve as the primary Career Development Center liaison and subject-matter resource for both the School of Public Service and School of Arts and Humanities maintaining expertise in career pathways, recruiting practices and timelines, employment trends, emerging roles, professional associations, skills, credentials, and experiential learning opportunities. Provide comprehensive career advising and coaching to students related to career exploration and decision-making, career readiness, professional skill development, networking, job and internship searches, and post-graduate planning. Partner with faculty and staff to develop and deliver discipline- and industry-specific career resources, programming, classroom presentations, and experiential learning opportunities. Connect students with employers, alumni, graduate/professional programs, and relevant career opportunities through targeted programming, communications, Handshake, and other Career Development Center resources. Ensure consistent and equitable access to career development support across assigned areas and serve as a back-up advisor for other Schools, majors, and industries as needed. Employer, Alumni, and Experiential Engagement Develop and sustain relationships with employers, alumni, and industry professionals within assigned areas through proactive outreach, networking, site visits, referrals, conferences, and other strategic engagement. Identify and cultivate internships, employment, job shadowing, project-based learning, mentorship, site visits, and other experiential opportunities aligned with student and institutional needs. Partner with campus stakeholders and faculty to expand regional and national employer and alumni engagement. Plan and execute employer-facing programs and recruiting initiatives, including industry-specific Meet and Greets, information sessions, site visits, and on-campus recruitment activities. Monitor industry trends, hiring practices, recruiting timelines, workforce needs, emerging occupations, and employer expectations; translate insights into advising, programming, faculty partnerships, and career readiness initiatives. Document employer and alumni engagement and partnership activity within designated Career Development Center systems to support coordinated outreach, assessment, and relationship management. Campus Career Ecosystem & Outcomes Advance the Elizabethtown College Career Action Plan within assigned areas by monitoring student engagement and using participation data to inform targeted outreach, programming, and continuous improvement. Partner with Institutional Research and campus stakeholders to support First Destination Survey data collection and analysis and identify opportunities to strengthen post-graduate outcomes. Collaborate with faculty and campus partners to integrate NACE career competencies, career readiness initiatives, and emerging credentialing or digital badging frameworks into the student experience. Develop partnerships with student organizations, academic departments, alumni, and employers and curate industry-specific resources to expand career education and industry engagement. Contribute to assessment, strategic planning, and continuous improvement efforts supporting Career Development Center and institutional priorities. Career Development Center Leadership & Operations Instruct CP 141 Mapping Career Goals 1 credit course each semester. Provide leadership for assigned Center-wide programs, initiatives, technologies, or functional areas based on departmental needs and areas of expertise. Collaborate with Career Development Center colleagues to ensure consistent service delivery, share industry knowledge, cross-train across assigned areas, and support Center-wide events and initiatives. Represent the Career Development Center on institutional committees, working groups, and initiatives and contribute to the training and supervision of student employees, interns, or Career Peers as assigned Requirements Education and/or Experience: MA or MS in Higher Education Administration, MA or MS in Counseling, or similar degree Career technology: Handshake or comparable career-services management/recruiting platforms Data and workflow tools: Microsoft Excel and Airtable or comparable database/project-management tools Career-readiness technology: Big Interview or comparable virtual interviewing/career-preparation platforms Learning management systems: Canvas or comparable LMS Productivity/collaboration: Microsoft 365, particularly Outlook, Teams, Word, PowerPoint, and Excel Virtual engagement: Zoom and/or Microsoft Teams Preferred Qualifications: A minimum of three years in Career Services, Employer Relations, and/or Alumni Relations Certificates, Licenses, and/or Registrations This position requires a valid driver’s license for business travel purposes (individual must have a US driver’s license for at least three years; a motor vehicle record check will be run and the incumbent must pass the College’s MVR rating system). For full consideration please provide cover letter, resume and contact information for (3) references."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3831869": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Cook. Elizabethtown College. Description Dining Services at Elizabethtown College is seeking (2) full-time Cooks. This role prepares and serves high-quality food throughout Elizabethtown College Dining Services while maintaining established standards for food safety, sanitation, quality, presentation, and customer service. Cooks may work in the Marketplace, residential dining, retail dining, Fresh Nest, the Food Truck, catering, or other Dining Services operations and may be cross-trained or assigned between locations based on operational needs. Employees are expected to learn and perform the responsibilities associated with their assigned location(s). Location-Specific Responsibilities Marketplace/Residential Dining Prepare food in appropriate quantities for high-volume residential dining service Follow production sheets, recipes, menus, and established production schedules Prepare and maintain food for assigned stations, including action/display cooking stations as applicable Monitor service levels and replenish food throughout meal periods while maintaining quality and presentation standards Adjust production based on guest counts, service volume, and available product to reduce shortages and excess production Properly cool, label, store, and document leftover food in accordance with established procedure Communicate production needs, shortages, substitutions, and other concerns to culinary leadership Jay's Nest & Food Truck Prepare made-to-order menu items accurately and efficiently in a high-volume retail environment Read and execute guest orders/tickets while maintaining appropriate speed of service and product quality Operate grills, fryers, ovens, and other equipment associated with assigned menu concepts Maintain adequate product levels and complete preparation necessary to support service Communicate with front-of-house employees to ensure order accuracy and timely service Assist with setup, breakdown, stocking, and cleaning of the Food Truck or retail operation as assigned Maintain organization and food safety standards in limited-space production environments Fresh Nest Prepare smoothies, açaí bowls, grab-and-go items, and other Fresh Nest menu offerings according to established recipes and portion standards Prepare and portion fruits, vegetables, bases, toppings, and other ingredients needed for service Maintain consistency in product appearance, portioning, and presentation Monitor ingredient levels, freshness, and quality throughout service Follow established procedures for allergen awareness and prevention of cross-contact Maintain cleanliness and sanitation of blenders, utensils, equipment, refrigeration, and food-contact surfaces Assist with preparation, packaging, labeling, and stocking of grab-and-go products as assigned Check out our perks! FREE undergraduate tuition for employee, spouse & dependents after six months of employment FREE access to Bowers Wellness Center (including FREE exercise classes & cardio/weight equipment & pool) FREE access to High Library Generous health, dental, vision & 401k plan match Paid time off between Christmas & New Years Day Generous vacation and sick leave Local Business discounts for Employees Uniforms (pants, shirts, shoes & hats provided) Staff receives one FREE meal per shift For full consideration please provide resume and contact information for (3) work related references. Elizabethtown College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by state or federal law Requirements Education and/or Experience High school diploma or GED is required. Associate’s degree from an accredited culinary institute is preferred; plus two years of food service experience; or equivalent combination of education and experience."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4313828": {
      "title": "ES Worker II",
      "description": "ES Worker II. Elizabethtown College. Description The Facilities Management department at Elizabethtown College is seeking (2) ES Workers (Level II) The following shifts are available: Monday-Friday 9:00pm-5:30am or Monday-Friday 6:00am-2:30pm, please indicate your preference when applying. The primary purpose of this position is to complete custodial and cleaning duties for all campus buildings while interacting positively with all members of the College. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Clean a variety of areas; including but not limited to; restrooms, shower areas, locker rooms, classrooms, offices, lounges, hallways, stairwells Perform routine floor care, i.e. vacuuming, dust mopping, wet mopping Collect trash/recycling from receptacles Report all vandalism and needed repairs to the Shift Supervisor Maintain all outside entrance areas free of debris and snow Complete bio-hazard clean-up training and provide this service The ability to work with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures Other duties as assigned, such as, but not limited to snow removal, set-ups, and grounds work NON-ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Must complete work in accordance to the Mission, Vision, and Values of the department and College Conduct all responsibilities in a safe manner according to regulations (OSHA, EPA, etc.) Other Skills, Abilities, and/or Training Ability to work extended hours as needed Ability to work weekends Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Good interpersonal skills and desire to be a team player Exceptional customer service skills Excellent oral communication skills (i.e. ability to deal effectively with others, speak professionally on the phone, etc.) PHYSICAL DEMANDS Rarely required to remain seated in a normal position for long periods of time Regularly required to walk about Regularly required to maintain balance while walking, standing, crouching, or running Regularly required to reach up and out with hands and arms Regularly required to talk and hear; verbally express information or instructions Regularly required to use hands to grasp objects, type, pick up objects, move objects, or hold objects Regularly required to stoop, kneel, crouch, and/or crawl Regularly required to climb stairs and/or ladders Occasionally required to lift up to 50 pounds and carry a distance of 10 feet Occasionally required to push and/or pull up to 50 pounds a distance of 10 feet Occasionally required to stand for long periods of time VISION REQUIREMENTS To successfully perform this position, individuals must possess the following: Close vision (clear vision at 20 inches or less) Depth perception and the ability to judge distances and spatial relationships Adjustable focus WORK ENVIRONMENT The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those encountered while performing the essential functions of this job. The individual is regularly exposed to indoor conditions, outdoor weather and temperature extremes, and moderate noise level. Elizabethtown College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by state or federal law Requirements Education and/or Experience High school diploma/GED. One to two years of custodial experience preferred Certificates, Licenses, and/or Registrations This position requires a valid driver’s license for business travel purposes (individual must have a US driver’s license for at least three years; a motor vehicle record check will be run and the incumbent must pass the College’s MVR rating system). For full consideration please provide, cover letter stating shift preference, resume and contact information for (3) work related references."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4528511": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty-Public Health",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty-Public Health. Elizabethtown College. Description The School of Public Service and the Public Health Program at Elizabethtown College, PA invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor to teach Introduction to Global Health . We are expanding our adjunct faculty pool and are seeking dynamic educators who bring both academic expertise and real-world industry experience to the classroom. This is a part-time position for the spring 2027 semester with potential for renewal based on performance and departmental needs. Candidates able to teach in-person are preferable, though remote instruction will be considered. Responsibilities: · Deliver engaging and effective instruction in global health lectures. · Prepare course materials and assessments aligned with departmental standards. · Provide timely feedback and support to students. · Collaborate with faculty and staff to support student success. Support for Teaching Development: At Elizabethtown College, we are committed to supporting excellence in teaching. Adjunct faculty have access to professional development opportunities, including workshops on evidence-based teaching practices, classroom technology, and mentorship from experienced faculty members. Requirements Education/Experience: Master’s degree in public health or related field or equivalent experience Demonstrated expertise in Global Health Commitment to inclusive and student-centered teaching practices Experience in developing online coursework in the area of global health will be considered. For full consideration, please submit the following: Cover letter outlining your teaching interests and relevant industry experience, if applicable Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy (optional but encouraged) Contact information for (3) professional references Please note, due to internal payroll limitations Elizabethtown College will only hire applicants residing in following states at this time: Pennsylvania Maine Maryland New Jersey North Carolina Virginia E lizabethtown College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by state or federal law."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4514604": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Communications",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Communications. Elizabethtown College. Description Elizabethtown College is seeking applicants for an Assistant Teaching Professor in Communications – Public Relations (non-tenure track). The Communications program is housed within the School of Public Service whose mission is grounded in the motto of Elizabethtown College, Educate for Service. Our programs empower students to use their knowledge, expertise, and communication skills to solve pressing problems in their communities and around the globe. This is a full-time, nine-month, on-campus position reporting to the Dean of the School of Public Service. The preferred start date is August 1, 2027. The College is looking to hire innovative faculty prepared to support our increasingly diverse student body. The School of Public Service faculty are committed to preparing students for lifelong learning, service, and professional outcomes. Approximately 30% of Elizabethtown College students are first-generation college students. We are looking for a Public Relations specialist with the ability to cover a range of courses within the program. Primary teaching responsibilities will include: Public Relations, PR Writing, Advanced PR, Organizational Communications, Feature Writing, and Senior Capstone. This position also serves as faculty advisor to Jay Firm, a student-run public relations and strategic communications agency. Candidates who have an interest in sports communications and sports PR are especially encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills and a commitment to collaboration. Experience with or demonstrated ability to teach, mentor, and support students from historically underrepresented groups is preferred. We prefer candidates with the ability to contribute to the diversity of our department and institution, whether through personal experience, teaching, scholarship, or service. Job Duties: Specific job responsibilities include teaching within the curriculum, participating in effective marketing and recruitment of undergraduate students to the program, advising and mentoring students, advising student research projects, providing service to the program, and making significant contributions to college-wide councils/committees. Requirements Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in communications, public relations or a related field with significant professional communications experience. Professional experience in public relations or strategic communications is required. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in communications or related field is preferred Previous teaching experience with evidence of student-centered approach Qualified applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, a narrative of practical experience, and contact & email addresses for three references. Summaries of previous teaching evaluations, if available, should be provided. The cover letter should detail your specific interest in being part of the Elizabethtown College community and how you will contribute to creating a diverse and inclusive environment. The teaching statement should detail a philosophy of teaching and emphasize strategies you will use to engage students. The narrative of practical experience should highlight how relevant work history and ongoing professional activity will enhance the teaching and advising of students. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until a successful candidate is found. Inquiries can be addressed to Dr. April Kelly (kellya@etown.edu) Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4302066": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Sport Medicine",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Sport Medicine. Elizabethtown College. Description The Exercise Science Department at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking an Adjunct Instructor-Exercise Science to teach our ESC 140 Sport Medicine course. The adjunct instructor will teach once section offered in Spring 2027 and potentially in the future depending on needs. This position is in-person, not remote. Adjunct faculty in exercise science are responsible for teaching students in undergraduate courses. Candidates must have the academic credentials to teach in one or more of the following areas: exercise physiology, exercise physiology lab, data collection and statistical analysis in exercise science, exercise testing and prescription, exercise and sport psychology, health and wellness promotion, and other potential courses and subjects. Part-time faculty must prepare and implement weekly lessons and lab activities, communicating with students via email and online announcements, be able to use the CANVAS online classroom platform, and provide grades and grade feedback within a timely fashion. Adjunct Faculty Teaching Responsibilities include: Teach material from the approved curriculum in accordance with the assigned schedule to ensure student satisfaction. Assist students in achieving completion of objectives and learning outcomes. Provide regular and timely feedback to students. Advice students in matters related to academics and attendance. Motivate students to actively participate in all aspects of the educational process. Maintain and report student grades and attendance in accordance with university policies. Other duties as assigned. For full consideration, please provide cover letter, CV and contact information for (3) professional references. Requirements Qualifications: M.S. or doctoral degree in Exercise Science or related field. Professional certification from NSCA, ACSM, or NATA. At a minimum, be able to teach sport medicine and health and wellness promotion. Preferred Qualifications: M.S. or Ph.D. in Athletic Training. Current active NATA-ATC certification. At least 2-years of hands-on clinical experience as an athletic trainer. Hold current valid state license to practice as an athletic trainer."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4495730": {
      "title": "PM Dining Services Supervisor",
      "description": "PM Dining Services Supervisor. Elizabethtown College. Description Dining Services at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking a PM Dining Services Supervisor . The PM Dining Services Supervisor is responsible for overseeing the evening closing procedures for all dining services operations and supervising the food truck. This position ensures that all end-of-shift duties are completed efficiently and in compliance with food safety and operational standards. The supervisor is also responsible for all food truck related events. The ideal candidate must be highly communicative, meticulously organized team player who possesses a positive, problem-solving attitude and a passion for innovation. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS PM Dining Services Supervisor Act as person in charge (PIC) during scheduled shift. Ensuring compliance with ServSafe guidelines and FDA Food Code regulations Monitor food handling, storage, and sanitation practices to maintain a safe dining environment Enforce health and safety policies and address any violations or concerns Ensure all closing tasks are completed, including, but not limited to: Trash removal Proper food storage and labeling Cleaning and shutting down all equipment Conduct end-of-day inspections to verify cleaning standards are met Check in with the night cleaning crew to review expectations and address any issues Oversee and verify that all cash drawers are balanced and properly closed Achieve personal and team goals as assigned Food Truck Supervisor Oversee daily operations of the food truck, including setup, service, and cleanup Utilize knives, cooking utensils, and all kitchen equipment effectively Maintain accurate inventory for the food truck and coordinate restocking as needed Work all food truck events, both on and off campus, ensuring efficient service and compliance with food safety regulations Support and supervise staff working in the food truck, providing guidance and troubleshooting issues as they arise Handle cash transactions, ensure proper change availability, and monitor cash drawer balances Maintain a clean and organized work environment, following “clean as you go” principles Adhere to and enforce food safety, sanitation, and equipment maintenance standards Ensure adequate staffing coverage, including coordinating break schedules Foster teamwork and a positive work environment, promoting quality service and communication within the dining services department Able to work with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures Other duties as assigned NON-ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Assist other areas within Dining Services Assist with cleaning and sanitation duties Attend conferences to further education Conduct all responsibilities in a safe manner according to regulations (OSHA, EPA, etc.) QUALIFICATIONS To perform this position successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential function satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made. Education and/or Experience High school diploma or GED is required. Associate degree from an accredited culinary institute is preferred; plus two years of food service supervisory experience; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Certificates, Licenses, and/or Registrations This position requires PA ServSafe certification and a valid driver’s license for business travel purposes (individual must have a US driver’s license for at least three years; a motor vehicle record check will be run and the incumbent must pass the College’s MVR rating system). Other Skills, Abilities, and/or Training Ability to drive and operate a mobile food kitchen Ability to work extended hours as needed Ability to work weekends Ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Ability to work within strict deadlines Good interpersonal skills and desire to be a team player Creative problem-solving skills Exceptional customer service skills Excellent oral communication skills (i.e. ability to deal effectively with others, speak professionally on the phone, etc.) Ability to read and communicate in English Able to operate register system and standard computer PHYSICAL DEMANDS Occasionally required to remain seated in a normal position for long periods of time Regularly required to walk about Regularly required to maintain balance while walking, standing, crouching, or running Regularly required to reach up and out with hands and arms Regularly required to talk and hear; verbally express information or instructions Regularly required to use hands to grasp objects, type, pick up objects, move objects, or hold objects Learn and follow all Serv Safe food safety and sanitation rules Regularly required to stoop, kneel, crouch, and/or crawl Regularly required to climb stairs and/or ladders Occasionally required to lift up to 50 pounds and carry a distance of 10 feet VISION REQUIREMENTS To successfully perform this position, individuals must possess the following: Close vision (clear vision at 20 inches or less) Depth perception and the ability to judge distances and spatial relationships Adjustable focus Ability to distinguish colors WORK ENVIRONMENT The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those encountered while performing the essential functions of this job. The individual is regularly exposed to indoor conditions and moderate noise level; the individual is occasionally exposed to outdoor weather and temperature extremes and chemicals/fumes associated with facility sanitation."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4470644": {
      "title": "Faculty Member- Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Faculty Member- Physician Assistant Program. Elizabethtown College. Description The Physician Assistant Program at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking a full-time Faculty member with duties to be performed on a twelve-month basis. This faculty member is responsible for teaching graduate-level courses for didactic and clinical year PA students in compliance with expectations set forth by ARC-PA accreditation standards and the NCCPA blueprint under the guidance of the Program Director. Primary responsibilities will be to didactic year students. Job Duties: · Provide graduate-level lecture and laboratory instruction to PA students · Assist the Program Director in the organization, administration, continuous and periodic review, planning, development and general effectiveness of the PA program · Develop, maintain, implement, evaluate, and ensure adequacy and appropriateness of assigned courses to ensure compliance with the ARC-PA standards · Participate in the accreditation process and assist in preparations for ARC-PA site visits · Evaluate student performance and competencies for assigned courses · Evaluate student performance and competencies during the didactic and clinical years · Participate in selecting applicants for admission to the PA program · Review course syllabi with all didactic instructors · Participate in reviewing and revising as necessary the mission statement for the program · Serve as an academic advisor to assist students in curriculum and career planning · Provide and maintain a reliable schedule of office hours for student advising, remediation, and consultation · Schedule and assist with formal student remediation in compliance with program expectations and accreditation standards, as needed · Participate in interprofessional education (IPE) programs for didactic and clinical year programs · Participate in ongoing evaluation of the PA program · Participate as a member of the Physician Assistant Faculty Committee and the Academic and Professional Affairs Committee · Maintain a professional development plan that addresses teaching, scholarship, service as well as diversity, equity, accessibility and justice to the standard performance expectations. Requirements Required Qualifications: · Graduate of ARC-PA accredited program or other associated accredited program specific to applicant’s discipline · Current NCCPA certification or current certification per applicant’s discipline · Master’s degree in Physician Assistant studies or related field · Eligible for licensure in Pennsylvania · Five or more years of clinical experience Preferred Qualifications: · Prior teaching experience in physician assistant education is preferred For full consideration, please provide cover letter, CV and contact information for (3) references."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3785580": {
      "title": "General Kitchen Utility Worker",
      "description": "General Kitchen Utility Worker. Elizabethtown College. Description Dining Services at Elizabethtown College is seeking (2) General Kitchen Utility Workers. Position #1 : Is a yearly 10-month role, mid-August through mid-May. Summers off! Position #2: is a yearly 12-month role. Please indicate which position you would prefer when applying. Full for consideration, please provide a resume and contact information for three references. The primary purpose of this position is to ensure proper cleaning, sanitation, and organization of all service ware, cooking utensils, and equipment for residential dining facilities, cash operations, and catered events. This position also supports overall kitchen cleanliness, including deep cleaning of kitchen floors, walk-ins, and workspaces. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Clean and sanitize all service ware, cooking utensils, and kitchen equipment Clean, sanitize, and maintain all beverage, waffle, and cereal equipment Preform dish room duties, including pre-rinsing dishware, washing flatware, plates, bowls and scrubbing pots and pans Clean and sanitize dining room tables and chairs Maintain adequate stock levels of dishes, flatware, beverage, cereal, waffle mix, and related items Utilize all equipment and chemicals safely and effectively Always maintain the highest levels of safety and sanitation Maintain sanitation and equipment records as required Maintain optimum station coverage at all times and cover for coworkers’ breaks and PTO Provide exceptional customer service Train student personnel Clean and maintain kitchen spaces, including floors, walk-in coolers, and prep areas Ensure all kitchen areas are properly closed, organized and ready for the following day’s operation Other duties as assigned NON-ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Assist in receiving deliveries and stocking inventory as required Assist in food production as required Conduct all responsibilities in a safe manner according to regulations (OSHA, EPA, etc.) QUALIFICATIONS To perform this position successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential function satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made. Education and/or Experience High school diploma or equivalent is required. Other Skills, Abilities, and/or Training Ability to work extended hours/overtime as needed Ability to work holidays Ability to work weekends Ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Ability to work within strict deadlines Good interpersonal skills and desire to be a team player Exceptional customer service skills Excellent oral communication skills (i.e. ability to deal effectively with others, speak professionally on the phone, etc.) Ability to read and communicate in English at a high school level PHYSICAL DEMANDS Regularly required to stand for long periods of time Regularly required to walk about Regularly required to maintain balance while walking, standing, crouching, or running Occasionally required to reach up and out with hands and arms Regularly required to talk and hear; verbally express information or instructions Regularly required to use hands to grasp objects, type, pick up objects, move objects, or hold objects Occasionally required to stoop, kneel, crouch, and/or crawl Regularly required to climb stairs and/or ladders Occasionally required to lift up to 50 pounds and carry a distance of 10 feet Occasionally required to push and/or pull up to 50 pounds a distance of 10 feet VISION REQUIREMENTS To successfully perform this position, individuals must possess the following: Close vision (clear vision at 20 inches or less) Depth perception and the ability to judge distances and spatial relationships Adjustable focus WORK ENVIRONMENT The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those encountered while performing the essential functions of this job. The individual is regularly exposed to indoor conditions and moderate noise level; the individual is occasionally exposed to outdoor weather and temperature extremes. The individual is occasionally exposed to chemicals and fumes related to facility sanitation. Elizabethtown College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by state or federal law"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4301724": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Engineering Mathematics",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Engineering Mathematics. Elizabethtown College. Description Elizabethtown College invites applications for a full-time Assistant Teaching Professor of Engineering Mathematics within the School of Engineering and Computer Science, beginning January or August 2027. This is a teaching-focused position supporting an Applied Calculus sequence, the foundational mathematics experience for Engineering and Computer Science students. This position will teach in-person classes. We seek an innovative and engaging educator with a strong background in mathematics education and student learning in quantitative disciplines, who is prepared to deliver calculus through applied, modeling-based, and student-centered approaches aligned with engineering and computing contexts. The ideal candidate will contribute to a collaborative teaching culture that emphasizes active learning, mastery-based assessment, and real-world application of mathematics. The School of Engineering and Computer Science offers an ABET-accredited multidisciplinary Engineering program and is nationally recognized for its mastery-based pedagogy and active engagement with the American Society for Engineering Education (ASEE) and the Kern Entrepreneurial Engineering Network (KEEN). Requirements Required Qualifications Master’s degree or higher (ABD, Ed.D. or Ph.D. preferred) with a focus in Mathematics Education or Engineering Education Experience teaching pre-calculus and calculus for Engineering majors. Formal graduate training in mathematics education research or engineering education research. Demonstrated use of active learning or mastery-based teaching practices. Experience assessing mathematics curricula and instructional techniques. Effective interpersonal and communication skills and ability to collaborate across disciplines. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate mathematics, particularly pre-calculus, Calculus I, and Calculus II, with an emphasis on student learning, conceptual understanding, and applied problem solving. Experience incorporating modeling, computational tools (e.g., Excel, MATLAB), or real-world applications into mathematics instruction. Engagement with KEEN (Kern Entrepreneurial Engineering Network) Experience supporting diverse learners and improving student persistence in STEM pathways. Familiarity with assessment of gateway mathematics courses. Teaching Responsibilities Instruction of approximately 16 contact hours per week, including multiple sections of first- and second-year Applied Calculus. Primary responsibility for teaching the Applied Calculus sequence. Coordination and continuous improvement of course content, instructional practices, and assessment within the Applied Calculus sequence. Potential to teach other courses aligned with elementary and secondary mathematics education. Additional Responsibilities Participation in Departmental, School, and institutional service, including shared governance and student recruitment activities. Contribution to ECS’s collaborative and innovative teaching culture. Ongoing engagement in professional development related to mathematics education and student learning in STEM. Application Instructions All applicants should submit a cover letter, CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. The cover letter (1-2 pages) should detail your specific interest in being a member of the Elizabethtown College community and discuss the unique values you would add to our educational experiences. The teaching statement (3 pages maximum) should detail a philosophy of teaching and emphasize strategies you will use to engage and support students. Three references will be contacted by Elizabethtown College. Salary and benefits will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Please note, due to the nature of this position, Elizabethtown College is not sponsoring visas for this position and will only consider US workers. Also, due to payroll tax limitations Elizabethtown College can only employ residents residing in one of the following states: Maryland, Maine, New Jersey, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Virginia. Elizabethtown College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by state or federal law"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4292353": {
      "title": "Assistant Swim Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Swim Coach. Elizabethtown College. Description The Athletic Department at Elizabethtown College is currently seeking a part-time Assistant Swim Coach. The Assistant Coach would aid the Head Coach with the organization and administration of the College’s intercollegiate Men’s & Women’s Swim programs. The individual will mentor, motivate, and develop student athletes in a Division III educational environment, assist the Head Coach in with practices, contests, recruitment and scouting. Work with students and staff from diverse backgrounds and ensure the athletic program is conducted in accordance with the NCAA and conference rules and regulations. Requirements: A bachelor’s degree plus 3-5 years of coaching experience, preferably on the college level, is preferred; or equivalent combination of education and experience. This position requires a valid driver’s license for business travel purposes (individual must have a US driver’s license for at least three years and also be qualified under College policy to transport students in college-owned and/or leased vehicles). CPR, AED and 1st Aid certification also is required. For full consideration, please provide cover letter, resume & contact information for (3) references. ACT153 are required for this position, if you have the following clearances (PA Child Abuse, PA State Police and FBI) please include them when applying. If not, the College will order them for you if an offer of employment is extended."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4207494": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Engineering. Elizabethtown College. Description The Elizabethtown College School of Engineering and Computer Science is seeking an individual passionate about multidisciplinary undergraduate engineering education to join our dynamic faculty team. We invite applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Engineering to begin in August 2027. This position may be filled on either a tenure-track or teaching professor (non-tenure) track depending on the applicants’ qualifications and interests. The position is full-time, nine months, and face-to-face (in-person) with rank determined based on qualifications. We seek an innovative and engaging faculty member able to teach introductory Electrical Engineering courses (including Circuits) and contribute to the development and instruction of upper-level courses in electrical-related engineering sciences aligned with their expertise. Candidates with proficiency in electrical engineering and expertise in fields including electrical, computer, materials, mechatronics, biomedical, robotics, engineering physics, or aerospace engineering backgrounds are encouraged to apply. The School of Engineering and Computer Science offers a multidisciplinary Engineering program with nine concentrations and is nationally recognized for its mastery-based pedagogy and active engagement with ASEE and the Kern Entrepreneurial Engineering Network (KEEN). Recently ranked in the top 20% of undergraduate-focused engineering programs nationwide (#46 tie) by U.S. News & World Report, the program continues to grow in reputation for producing technically strong, socially responsible, and entrepreneurially minded graduates. Required Qualifications Tenure-Track Faculty (Assistant or Associate Professor) Requires a Ph.D. awarded by August 2027 in an engineering discipline (e.g., Electrical or related field such as Computer, Materials, Biomedical, Mechatronics, Engineering Physics, or Aerospace Engineering). Expected to develop and maintain an undergraduate-centered technical engineering research agenda consistent with Etown’s scale and teaching mission Typical load: 12 contact hours per week , including class sessions, labs, and project supervision. Expected to teach Circuits and develop 1–2 upper-level electrical or related undergraduate courses in their area of expertise. Teaching Professor (Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor) Requires a Master’s degree or higher in engineering or a closely related field , with industry experience preferred. No research expectations. Typical load: 15 contact hours per week, including class sessions, labs, and project supervision. Primarily focused on introductory-level courses and labs in Electrical Engineering and related fields but may include instruction in upper-level undergraduate coursework. Both positions require a commitment to excellence in undergraduate education and collaboration as well as effective interpersonal and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated ability to teach, mentor, and support students; A demonstrated ability to incorporate active learning, project-based learning or other evidence-based teaching practices, which may include engagement with KEEN and ASEE; A demonstrated ability to involve undergraduate students in research; A multidisciplinary background enabling wide coverage of engineering courses. Job Duties Teaching undergraduate engineering and physics courses and labs that may include Circuits, Physics II (electromagnetism), upper-level electrical-related engineering electives, Introduction to Engineering, and Capstone Design. Advising and mentoring undergraduate engineering students. Serving the Department, School, and Institution, including interaction with prospective students and families, participation in ABET accreditation processes, and engagement with institutional shared governance. Contribute to ECS’s collaborative and innovative teaching culture. Maintain and implement professional development plan. For tenure-track candidates: Conduct scholarly activities leading to publication/presentation, particularly engineering sciences work in collaboration with undergraduate research students. Application Instructions All applicants should submit a cover letter, CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. Tenure-track candidates must also submit a research statement; teaching-track candidates are not required to do so. The cover letter (1-2 pages) should detail your specific interest in being a member of the Elizabethtown College community and discuss the unique values you would add to our educational experiences. The teaching statement (3 pages maximum) should detail a philosophy of teaching and emphasize strategies you will use to engage and support students. Contact information for three references who will be contacted by the Search Chair. Tenure-track candidates only: The research statement (2 pages maximum) should address your plans for leading and publishing engineering sciences research at Elizabethtown College and explain how you might involve undergraduate students. Applications received by September 15, 2026, will receive full consideration. Salary and benefits will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Please note, due to payroll limitations employees of the college must reside in one of the following states: MD, ME, NJ, NC, PA & VA Elizabethtown College is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by state or federal law."
    }
  },
